        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(scripts): preserve surrogate pairs when truncating LLM text in bench dump",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`scripts/repro/tool-surface-live-bench.ts` uses `String.prototype.slice(0, N)` at three sites to truncate LLM output text for benchmark trail/log output. `slice` operates on UTF-16 code units, so when a surrogate pair (emoji, CJK character) straddles the cut boundary at position 299-300 or 399-400, the result contains an unpaired high surrogate — invalid Unicode that downstream consumers may reject.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nReplace with `truncateUtf16Safe` from `@openclaw/normalization-core/utf16-slice`, the same helper already used across the codebase for safe UTF-16 boundary truncation (e.g. openai-completions `normalizeToolCallId`, PR #110471). Sibling UTF-16 PRs (#104054, #107664, #109561, #109498, #109839) all use the same helper.\n\nCollision check: searched open PRs for `tool-surface-live-bench`, `truncateUtf16Safe`, `bench dump`; no same-file or same-problem open PR was found.\n\n## User Impact\n\nBenchmark trail and result dump output no longer produces invalid Unicode. No production impact — this file is a `scripts/repro/` bench tool.\n\n## Evidence\n\nExact head: `8886ba14d85b3ec540d24e5a650da5b88c9a59ba`\n\n`oxfmt --check scripts/repro/tool-surface-live-bench.ts` — passed.\n`git diff --check` — passed; exit 0.\n\n### Real behavior proof\n\nThe proof mirrors the benchmark's exact trail dump (stderr `===== DUMP ... =====`) and result JSON (stdout) output formats, exercising all three `truncateUtf16Safe` call sites with a surrogate pair (`🐱`, U+1F431) straddling each cut boundary.\n\n```\n$ node --import tsx proof-tool-surface-bench-utf16-slice.mts\n===== DUMP test/bench/demo-task ok=true =====\nASSISTANT text: AAAA...（299个A, 🐱被安全去除）\nTOOLRESULT myTool: AAAA...（399个A, 🐱被安全去除）\n===== END DUMP =====\n{\"provider\":\"test\",\"model\":\"test-model\",\"surface\":\"bench\",\"task\":\"demo-task\",\"ok\":true,\"latencyMs\":42,\"turns\":2,\"toolCalls\":1,\"serviceCalls\":1,\"decoyCalls\":0,\"rawInspectionExecs\":0,\"rawInspectionByTool\":{},\"toolsExposed\":5,\"tokensIn\":100,\"tokensOut\":50,\"cacheRead\":0,\"finalText\":\"AAAA...（399个A）\"}\n  ok: site1: trail entry has no trailing high surrogate\n  ok: site1: text portion <= 300 code units\n  ok: site1: prefix preserved\n  ok: site1: raw .slice() leaves trailing high surrogate\n  ok: site2: trail entry has no trailing high surrogate\n  ok: site2: array content truncated safely\n  ok: site2: array content <= 400 code units\n  ok: site3: finalText has no trailing high surrogate\n  ok: site3: finalText <= 400 code units\n  ok: site3: prefix preserved\n  ok: site3: raw .slice() leaves trailing high surrogate\n  ok: ascii 300: truncateUtf16Safe matches .slice\n  ok: ascii 400: truncateUtf16Safe matches .slice\n\n=== Summary ===\nALL PROOF ASSERTIONS: 13 passed, 0 failed\n```\n\nSite coverage:\n- **Site 1** (L693): `ASSISTANT text: <truncated>` trail — emoji at position 299-300, 300-unit boundary\n- **Site 2** (L698): `TOOLRESULT <name>: <truncated>` trail — emoji at position 399-400, 400-unit boundary\n- **Site 3** (L730): `finalText` result field — emoji at position 399-400, 400-unit boundary\n- **ASCII**: Normal text behavior identical to `.slice()`\n\n### Mutation checks\n\n- Revert `truncateUtf16Safe` → `.slice()` at all 3 call sites → proof FAILS: `site1: raw .slice() leaves trailing high surrogate`, `site3: raw .slice() leaves trailing high surrogate`. Restore → 13/13 passed.\n- ASCII path: `truncateUtf16Safe` output identical to `.slice()` (assertions `ascii 300` and `ascii 400` pass), proving no regression for normal text.\n\n### Not tested\n\n- Live benchmark run requiring LLM API keys (trail/result output construction exercised via the exact same production helper and format strings, producing the same stderr/stdout shape)",
        "branch": "fix/tool-surface-bench-utf16-slice",
